# Google Maps (optional)
#
# The app uses Google Maps for every map when a key is present, and falls back
# to the built-in keyless Leaflet/OpenStreetMap provider when it is not. So you
# can clone the repo and run `npm run dev` with this file absent — you just get
# OpenStreetMap tiles instead.
#
# To enable Google Maps:
#   1. Enable the "Maps JavaScript API" AND the "Places API (New)" for a Google
#      Cloud project (billing must be enabled on the project). The map renders
#      with the first; place search ("good flippin' burgers vasai" →
#      "GOOD FLIPPIN' BURGERS®, Vasai West") needs the second. Without it,
#      search silently falls back to the keyless Nominatim/Photon cascade,
#      which cannot fuzzy-match business names.
#   2. Create an API key and RESTRICT it:
#        - API restriction  -> "Maps JavaScript API" + "Places API (New)"
#        - Website restriction -> your origins, e.g. http://localhost:3000/*
#      Never ship an unrestricted key. The map key is visible in the client
#      bundle by design, so the restriction is what protects the quota. Place
#      search goes through the same-origin `/api/places-search` proxy, so the
#      key authorising it is never exposed beyond what the map already needs.
#   3. Copy this file to `.env.local` and paste the key in.
#
# For testing on a phone via `npm run dev:tunnel`, the Cloudflare hostname
# changes on every run, so a referrer-restricted key will be rejected. Temporarily
# set the website restriction to `*`, then restore it before deploying.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Cloud map ID for Google Maps. Required for AdvancedMarkerElement (the app's
# HTML pins); it refuses to load without one. `DEMO_MAP_ID` is Google's
# testing value and is applied automatically when this is empty, but it uses a
# reduced-POI style — create a real map ID (Map type: JavaScript) for production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_MAP_ID=